# How a resident feels about a player, in what they say to them (Docs/Design/62-talk.md, phase 7; "Players, as
# settled"): their disposition (hostile, wary, cool, neutral, warm, fond: from what the two have been through), what
# they've heard said of them, a long absence, and how the resident is today (grieving, hurt). These concepts always take
# their best tier: hostility always shows (priority 3); fondness, wariness and what's rumoured join the tone's own lines
# (the same score), so they come up often but not always; a resident's grief or hurt likewise.
#
# Never #other.name# here: a resident knows a player only by a name they were given (#topic.player#, doc 32).

## Greetings

rule rg_greet_hostile
when concept=player.greet pair.disposition=hostile
priority 3
say You. | I've nothing to say to you. | Keep walking. | What do you want? | Not you again.

rule rg_greet_hostile_named
when concept=player.greet pair.disposition=hostile topic.meeting=known|returning
priority 3
say #topic.player#. You've a nerve. | Oh, it's you, #topic.player#. Wonderful. | I know you, #topic.player#. Don't think I don't. | #topic.player#. I'd hoped you'd gone for good.

rule rg_greet_wary
when concept=player.greet pair.disposition=wary topic.meeting=known|returning
priority 1
say Oh. It's you. | What is it this time, #topic.player#? | #topic.player#. Hm. What do you want? | I'll keep my distance, #topic.player#, if it's all the same.

rule rg_greet_cool
when concept=player.greet pair.disposition=cool topic.meeting=known|returning
priority 1
say #topic.player#. | Aye, #topic.player#? | Back again. | #greet#. Was there something?

rule rg_greet_warm
when concept=player.greet pair.disposition=warm topic.meeting=known|returning
priority 1
say #topic.player#! Good to see you. | Ah, #topic.player#. There's a face I like. | Well met, #topic.player#. | #greet#, #topic.player#! You're looking well.

rule rg_greet_fond
when concept=player.greet pair.disposition=fond topic.meeting=known|returning
priority 1
say #topic.player#! There you are! | Oh, it's good to see you, #topic.player#. | My favourite face! #greet#, #topic.player#! | #topic.player#, #pet#! Come here.

rule rg_greet_long_gone
when concept=player.greet topic.meeting=returning pair.days_since>=28
priority 1
say #topic.player#! I thought you'd gone for good. | Where've you been all this while? It's been since #topic.since#! | Look what the wind blew in. It's been an age. | I'd near forgotten your face, #topic.player#. Near.

rule rg_greet_fond_long_gone
when concept=player.greet topic.meeting=returning pair.days_since>=28 pair.disposition=fond|warm
priority 1
say #topic.player#! I'd given you up! Where have you been? | Gods, #topic.player#! Not a word since #topic.since#! Come here. | You're back! I was sure something had happened to you. | There you are! I asked after you at the inn. Twice.

rule rg_greet_thief
when concept=player.greet pair.rumour=thief pair.disposition!=warm|fond
priority 1
say I'll keep a paw on my purse, if it's all the same. | I've heard about you. Hands where I can see them. | #greet#. I'm watching my things, mind. | They say you've light paws. We'll see.

rule rg_greet_violent
when concept=player.greet pair.rumour=violent pair.disposition!=warm|fond
priority 1
say Easy. I've heard what you did. | #greet#. No trouble, now. I want no trouble. | Stay where you are. Please. | They say you've a temper. I'll not test it.

rule rg_greet_promises
when concept=player.greet pair.rumour=breaks_promises pair.disposition!=warm|fond
priority 1
say Oh, it's you. The one whose word's worth nothing. | #greet#. Don't promise me anything. | I've heard about you and promises.

rule rg_greet_owed
when concept=player.greet pair.owed=b topic.meeting=known|returning
priority 1
say #topic.player#. Have you brought what you owe me? | #greet#, #topic.player#. You know what I'm going to say. | Ah. My debtor. How's my money?

rule rg_greet_mourning
when concept=player.greet mourning=kin
priority 2
say Oh. Hello. Forgive me, I'm not myself. | #greet#. It's been a hard week. | Hello. Sorry. We've had a death. | Forgive me. I've just buried one of mine.

rule rg_greet_hurt
when concept=player.greet injured=bad
priority 2
say Mind, don't jostle me. I'm hurt. | #greet#. Excuse me if I don't get up. | Ah. Hello. Gently, now. | Mind the leg. Hello.

rule rg_greet_robbed
when concept=player.greet robbed=yes
priority 2
say Hello. Watch your purse. I've been robbed. | Did you see anyone running? They robbed me! | #greet#. Sorry. Someone's had my things. | Robbed! Today! Have you seen a wolf with my purse?

## Thanks, and goodbye

rule rg_thanks_hostile
when concept=player.thanks pair.disposition=hostile
priority 3
say Hmph. | Don't thank me. Just go. | Aye. Now leave me be. | Keep your thanks.

rule rg_thanks_wary
when concept=player.thanks pair.disposition=wary
say Mm. | Aye, well. | Don't make a habit of it.

rule rg_thanks_warm
when concept=player.thanks pair.disposition=warm
say You're welcome, #topic.player#. | Glad to, glad to. | Any time. I mean it.

rule rg_thanks_fond
when concept=player.thanks pair.disposition=fond
say For you? Any time. | Oh, hush. You'd do the same for me. | Anything, #topic.player#. | Don't you dare thank me. Not you.

rule rg_bye_hostile
when concept=player.bye pair.disposition=hostile
priority 3
say Good riddance. | Don't come back. | Finally. | Go on. Go.

rule rg_bye_wary
when concept=player.bye pair.disposition=wary topic.meeting=known|returning
priority 1
say Mm. | Aye, go on. | Off you go, then. | Mind how you go. Far away.

rule rg_bye_cool
when concept=player.bye pair.disposition=cool topic.meeting=known|returning
priority 1
say Aye. | #farewell#. | Right, then.

rule rg_bye_warm
when concept=player.bye pair.disposition=warm topic.meeting=known|returning
priority 1
say Mind how you go, #topic.player#. | Come back soon, now. | Safe roads to you, #topic.player#.

rule rg_bye_fond
when concept=player.bye pair.disposition=fond topic.meeting=known|returning
priority 1
say Don't be a stranger, #topic.player#. | Come back soon, #pet#. | Safe roads, #topic.player#. Mind you come back. | Off you go, then. Don't leave it so long.

## What they're asked: the answer, but grudgingly (or gladly)

rule rg_answer_hostile
when concept=player.trade|player.hours|player.job|player.where|player.wanted|player.day pair.disposition=hostile
priority 3
say If you must know: #topic.answer# | #topic.answer# Now go. | Fine. #topic.answer# | #topic.answer# Don't ask me anything else.

rule rg_answer_wary
when concept=player.trade|player.hours|player.job|player.where|player.wanted|player.day pair.disposition=wary
priority 1
say Why do you ask? ... #topic.answer# | Hm. #topic.answer# | #topic.answer# That's all I know. | I suppose there's no harm. #topic.answer#

rule rg_answer_warm
when concept=player.trade|player.hours|player.job|player.where|player.wanted|player.day pair.disposition=warm
priority 1
say Happy to help, #topic.player#. #topic.answer# | Course. #topic.answer# | Let me think. Aye. #topic.answer#

rule rg_answer_fond
when concept=player.trade|player.hours|player.job|player.where|player.wanted|player.day pair.disposition=fond
priority 1
say For you? #topic.answer# | Anything for you. #topic.answer# | Oh, easy. #topic.answer# | You only had to ask. #topic.answer#
